"<p>Nitrobase provides first-class support for self-hosting the complete <strong>Supabase</strong> stack directly from official <code>supabase/supabase</code> monthly releases (<code>v1.YY.MM</code>), which pin a tested set of container images.</p>\n<h2>What Nitrobase Provisions</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>PostgreSQL + pgvector + Supavisor:</strong> Full Postgres engine with extensions and connection pooling.</li>\n<li><strong>Kong API Gateway, GoTrue Auth, PostgREST, Realtime, Storage, Edge Functions, and Supabase Studio.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Zero demo secrets:</strong> Upstream <code>.env.example</code> provides defaults, and Nitrobase overrides every insecure demo secret with cryptographically generated values—including <code>POSTGRES_PASSWORD</code>, <code>JWT_SECRET</code>, HS256 <code>ANON_KEY</code>/<code>SERVICE_ROLE_KEY</code>, and Studio credentials.</li>\n<li><strong>Asymmetric ES256 API keys (v1.26.04+):</strong> For Supabase <code>v1.26.04</code> and newer, Nitrobase automatically generates the new <code>SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY</code> (<code>sb_publishable_...</code>), <code>SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY</code> (<code>sb_secret_...</code>), ES256 <code>JWT_KEYS</code>/<code>JWT_JWKS</code>, and <code>ANON_KEY_ASYMMETRIC</code>/<code>SERVICE_ROLE_KEY_ASYMMETRIC</code>, and applies <code>overlay-api-keys.yml</code> to enable asymmetric JWT verification while keeping legacy keys working.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Built-in Supabase Provider Plugin</h2>\n<p>Nitrobase's Supabase plugin adds dedicated management tabs directly on your Supabase app page:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Edge Functions:</strong> Upload, edit, and deploy edge functions (up to <code>50</code> files and <code>1 MB</code> per function by default) and manage encrypted edge function secrets (<code>service-env/functions.env</code>, mode <code>0600</code>, up to <code>100</code> variables). Includes an HTTP invoke tester through the app's API gateway.</li>\n<li><strong>SQL Runner:</strong> Execute SQL directly inside the Postgres container (<code>app.database</code> permission, <code>30s</code> statement timeout, audited).</li>\n<li><strong>Storage Repair:</strong> Batch-check and repair storage file metadata (<code>SUPABASE_STORAGE_REPAIR_BATCH=1000</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Backups:</strong> Consistent <code>pg_dumpall</code> database dumps (taken after writer services stop) combined with storage volumes in a single <code>.tar.zst</code> archive.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Resource Recommendations</h2>\n<p>A full Supabase stack typically consumes <strong>1–1.5 GB of RAM</strong> at rest, so a <strong>2 GB+ RAM</strong> VPS (with swap enabled) is recommended.</p>"